->\n  `zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` ->\n  `pe.version_original_filename` -> `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` ->\n  `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`. The question literally names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`);\n  ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`); `dNN` = the member family's first day, not today.\n- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys and promises extra findings (\"find the collision\", \"the impossible\n  destination\", \"the document reaching somewhere it should not\") that were NEVER asked. The graded field is always the\n  STRUCTURAL truth from header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie.\n- Singles: D1-D9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13 and D15 each lost ONE submit to a spelling/ordering convention\n  (padding, braces, list order). Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT on its first GM submit (D15 TT after an offline\n  generalize for the new synthesis question).\n- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE). Pre-arm siblings\n  (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing spellings. Titles are puns, not format hints (D7 \"Seven-Zip\" was ZIP).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\"; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives. Container\n  NAMES drift too: D1-D14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`; D15 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding\n  `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n- **Field-set size** -- grows AND shrinks per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 single\n  1 vs TT 20 vs Mastery 100. Families: the day's field + identity + carry-overs `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`,\n  `d07-zip-*` (eocd + CD names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, version OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`,\n  `d14-lnk-*`, `d15-ooxml-*`. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX; keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference:\n  `challenges/day15/metadata-a-word-to-the-wise/solver/solve.py` answers all 20 + synthesis).\n- **Identity member roster** (D15 new) -- the kit now holds THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B,\n  `evidence-note-copy.txt` 33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B) and EACH identity question picks one at random per set:\n  ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` (`roster-sha1`,\n  `evidence-note-copy-filename`...). The filename question has artifact = the container only and asks \"the exact\n  filename of the roster\" -> map the id stem to the member whose stem matches. Never assume `evidence-note-*`.\n- **Synthesis / cross-member questions** (D15 new) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order`, kind `json`, norm\n  `case_insensitive`: \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of their\n  filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". The `artifact` names only ONE member; the real inputs are the\n  `Files:` JSON list in the question text, all in the same container. Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, resolve each\n  name under the ref's container, `hashlib.new(algo)` over the raw member bytes, sort by hex digest (descending only if\n  the text says so), emit names. Expect siblings (md5/sha1 order, size order) -- parse the algo from the id/text.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree with the\n  header: always answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names.\n- **Member values** -- re-roll per variant; never cache across sets. Seen: note case id (all days); D7 entry count\n  2/3/4/5; jpg/png dimensions (D15 every set different, e.g. 423x1089, 1255x1059); D10 entry RVA; D11 PE architecture\n  (386 0x014c / amd64 0x8664 / arm64 0xaa64, OriginalFilename `pe-base-<goarch>.exe` follows); D12 MVID; D15 synthesis\n  order (driven by the re-rolled note/jpg hashes). Constant so far but don't rely on it: D13 ProductCode (identical in\n  every mode -- \"collision\" by design), D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, the D15 kit's exe/dll/msi/lnk.\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per\n  `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions.\n- **Question-text tags** -- D9 TT/Mastery appended ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` to the first question; D15\n  timed questions are prefixed ``Inspect `<member>`. `` Strip both before reading names; route by id + `artifact`.\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer\n  from an enclosing zip. An OOXML member is itself a zip -- parse it as the asked member, not as a wrapper to descend.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |\n| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored path, CD order, no dedupe/sort; UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else UTF-8-then-cp437 |\n| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |\n| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |\n| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| `elf.*` / `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | ELF `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O `feedface`/`feedfacf` cputype @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 |\n| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` (HeapSizes @+6, Valid @+8, rows @+24) -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |\n| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB streams -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property` (column-major). `olefile` in venv; `day13/.../solve.py msi_property` |\n| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |\n| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | it's a zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part (`_rels/.rels`, `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`, header/footer/settings rels). External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship`. Core props (`docProps/core.xml`) prebuilt in `lib/meta/prebuilt/ooxml.py`; external rels NOT prebuilt as of D15 |\n| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |\n| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |\n| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`; decide ORDER per field (conventions) |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |\n\n## Day by day\n**Days 1-8** (one field each, first try ~27-57 s): D1 identity (Mastery zip-of-zips first seen) -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16`\n(TT `readme.exe` was text) -> D3 `text.utf8_bom_present` -> D4 JPEG SOFn `<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6\n`pdf.header_version` bare `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 `zip.central_directory_member_names`\ncompact JSON in CD order (5-member kit, 12 fields).\n\n**Days 9-11** (one Go PE, `d09-pe-NNN-...`): D9 `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c` (~47 s). D10\n`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` `0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED, ~75 s). D11 `pe.version_original_filename` verbatim\n(`pe-base-386.exe`, ~25 s). All TT/Mastery first try.\n\n**Days 12-14** (one new member family each, 1 field everywhere, TT 1 / Mastery 2x1, all timed first try):\nD12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` -- 5 KB .NET dll, #GUID heap -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le)` lowercase no braces, ~55 s. D13\n`msi.product_code_guid` -- 9.7 KB MSI, Property table ProductCode VERBATIM with braces (brace-less REJECTED), ~76 s. D14\n`lnk.target_path_windows` -- 547 B LNK, LinkInfo LocalBasePath `C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe`, ~40 s (prebuilt key was\n`target_path`, one suffix short -> worker re-typed the parser).\n\n**Day 15 — A Word to the Wise** (`ooxml.external_relationship_targets`, kind `json` \"compact valid JSON array with exact\nvalues and order\", norm `trim`, id `d15-ooxml-001-ooxml-external-relationship-targets`). Prompt: \"Office documents\ncontain relationships that point beyond the page. Separate internal references from external dependencies and find\nthe document reaching somewhere it should not.\"\n- Artifact: 1,316 B zip -> `document-15-001.docx` (3,803 B; 5 parts: `[Content_Types].xml`, `_rels/.rels`,\n  `docProps/core.xml`, `word/document.xml`, `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`). The package rels are Internal\n  (officeDocument, core-properties); `document.xml.rels` holds two `hyperlink` rels `rId9` -> `https://example.test/\n  evidence/<token>` and `rId10` -> `https://example.test/control`, both `TargetMode=\"External\"`, referenced from\n  `<w:hyperlink r:id=..>` in body order rId9, rId10.\n- Key insight: answer = the Target strings of every External relationship, as a compact JSON array SORTED ASCENDING\n  (`[\"https://example.test/control\",\"https://example.test/evidence/<token>\"]`). The rels-file / body order (rId9 first)\n  was REJECTED. Caveat: sorted-by-Target and sorted-by-Id-as-string (`rId10` < `rId9`) coincide here -- sort by Target.\n- Single: start -> wrong submit at +24 s (file order) -> CORRECT at +50 s. 1 wrong, ~26 s lost.\n- TT: the 12-member kit (note, `evidence-note-copy.txt`, `roster.csv`, jpg, png, pdf, evidence-drop zip, exe, dll, msi,\n  lnk, docx) with 20 fields incl. the new identity-member roster and `metadata-day-15-synthesis-sha256-order`. The\n  shipped solver didn't answer the synthesis id; offline generalize added `_digest_order` (above). TT CORRECT 20/20,\n  in-window 1.72 s (solve 0.27 s). Mastery 5 sets x 20 = 100 CORRECT first submit, in-window 1.83 s (solve 0.44 s).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase `x`, no spaces.\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:\n  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).\n  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.\n  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15 TT/Mastery; norm `case_insensitive`).\n  Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk\n  order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.\n- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine\n  `0x014c`, u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT, not the id. (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`;\n  the binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)\n- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces\n  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes).\n- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension.\n- URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups.\n- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15).\n- `knowledge.py` holds the format constants (`JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT` ... `PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT`, `DOTNET_MVID_GUID`,\n  `MSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID`, `LNK_TARGET_PATH_WINDOWS`, `BOOL`); `playbook` metadata entries carry hex/guid/path rules.\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,\n  `external_relationship_targets` = rels `Target` where `TargetMode=External`) -- read it literally to pick the\n  structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only).\n- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15 `evidence-01.zip`)\n  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15 five full kits, D15 ~606 KB\n  each). Refs `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member).\n- Mastery day 9: download named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not its filename.\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) -- never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- JSON list ORDER (D15, 1 wrong + ~26 s): \"exact values and order\" does not say WHICH order. File order was rejected\n  for rels targets; sorted won. Decide per field (conventions above) before the first submit.\n- Timed field set != single field set (D15): single asked 1 field, TT 20 incl. an unseen synthesis question and\n  re-rolled identity members -> the shipped solver missed one id. Keep the cumulative solver (identity for ANY member\n  stem, every carry-over family) in place before the timed run, and treat any `synthesis`/\"Files: [...]\" question as\n  a computed cross-member answer, not a lookup.\n- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") -- recurse.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (D2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: only the named field is graded; extra checks are diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded zip reads the OUTER EOCD. Resolve the named\n  member's bytes first, then parse (same for OOXML: open the docx member, not the evidence zip).\n- Name-list fields: emit CD bytes as-is for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `\\`, duplicates) -- extractors sanitize.\n- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF -- bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D15 start 1.0 s + submit 1.1 s). Parse in memory, never\n  shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member) (1.2 MB exe x5).\n- A prebuilt registry key one suffix short is a miss (D14 `lnk.target_path` vs `target_path_windows`). Check\n  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and call the nearest\n  extractor directly before writing one.\n- Fresh member family = copy the previous day's solver first (it answers every earlier family), then add only the new\n  handler -- D8 27 s / D9 47 s that way; re-typing older branches cost D12 ~50 s.\n- Normalizing a stored value (D13): don't strip braces/reshape a stored string because answer_format sounds generic.\n- Hex width (D10): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x`. `_rva` = raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n- Executable fields: the metadata field is the raw u16, not `file`/`pefile`/GOARCH names; require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew.\n- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` but NO `answer_ids`.\n- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on a solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` (D2, ~2 min lost) --\n  restore from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,\n  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile. Not installed: msitools, LnkParse3, dnfile.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":229,"newStart":1,"newLines":188,"lines":["-# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-14; updated after every day)","+# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-15; updated after every day)"," "," How this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a","   guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.","-- Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny","-  member (33 B - 3 KB) and ONE structural fact. Day 8+: the zip carries the whole cumulative kit (note + jpg + png + pdf +","-  inner zip [+ D9 a 1.26 MB PE `.exe`]) and even the SINGLE contract asks every field (D8 12, D9 13 = identity + every","-  earlier day's field + the new one). The member can itself be a container (D7/8: an inner ZIP whose own EOCD / CD is","-  the asked field). Each day adds ONE member + ONE field; the previous kit members are byte-identical except the case id.","-- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only","-  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`). Day 10 stayed on the SAME","-  PE (`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`) and DE-escalated: zip = the exe only, contract = 1 field (TT 1, Mastery 2x1).","-  Day 11 kept that shape and moved INTO the PE's resources (`pe.version_original_filename`, VS_VERSIONINFO string).","-  Day 12 switched to a NEW member family -- a 5 KB .NET dll (`d12-dotnet-NNN-dotnet-mvid-guid`) -- and went into the CLI","-  METADATA tables (Module.Mvid via the #GUID heap); same 1-field / TT 1 / Mastery 2x1 shape. Day 13 another NEW","-  family -- a 9.7 KB MSI (OLE/CFB, `d13-msi-NNN-msi-product-code-guid`) -> the Property table; same 1-field shape.","-  Day 14 another NEW family -- a 547 B Windows shortcut (`d14-lnk-NNN-lnk-target-path-windows`) -> LinkInfo; same shape.","-- A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->","+- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny member and ONE structural fact.","+  Day 8-9: the zip carries the whole cumulative kit and every mode asks every field (D9 13). Days 10-14 DE-escalated to","+  one member + one field in every mode (TT 1, Mastery 2x1). **Day 15 split the modes**: single = 1 field (the new","+  docx), but TT = the 12-member cumulative kit with 20 fields and Mastery = 5 kits x 20 = 100 -- incl. a brand-new","+  cross-member \"synthesis\" question. Always pre-arm every earlier family; the timed field set is not the single's.","+- Member families so far: note/text -> jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE `.exe` (D9-11) -> .NET dll (D12) -> MSI","+  (D13) -> LNK (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15). Each new family arrives with its own `dNN` id prefix.","+- A new `<fmt>.<field>` each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->","   `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` ->","   `zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` ->","-  `pe.version_original_filename` -> `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows`. Since Day 3 the question literally names the field","-  (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`). NOTE the","-  `dNN` is the drop/member family, not the day the field appeared: Day 8's new field came as `d07-zip-001-zip-central-","-  directory-member-names`; Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`); Day 10's as `d09-pe-001-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex` (same exe family), Day 11's as","-  `d09-pe-001-pe-version-original-filename`, Day 12's as `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid` (new family -> new `dNN`).","-- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk","-  \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides, \"impossible provenance\" names). The asked field so far was always the","-  STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Singles D1-D9 were","-  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; D10 took one wrong spelling (unpadded hex). Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT first try.","-- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9: \"executables for several architectures, plus decoys wearing","-  executable extensions\" -> one honest i386 PE, no ELF/Mach-O/decoy in any mode). Expect the promised cases to arrive","-  later as mutations; pre-arm the sibling parsers (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing their spellings.","-- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.","+  `pe.version_original_filename` -> `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` ->","+  `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`. The question literally names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`);","+  ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`); `dNN` = the member family's first day, not today.","+- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys and promises extra findings (\"find the collision\", \"the impossible","+  destination\", \"the document reaching somewhere it should not\") that were NEVER asked. The graded field is always the","+  STRUCTURAL truth from header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie.","+- Singles: D1-D9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13 and D15 each lost ONE submit to a spelling/ordering convention","+  (padding, braces, list order). Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT on its first GM submit (D15 TT after an offline","+  generalize for the new synthesis question).","+- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE). Pre-arm siblings","+  (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing spellings. Titles are puns, not format hints (D7 \"Seven-Zip\" was ZIP)."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)","-- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.","-- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree","-  with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.","-- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is","-  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`). Day 8 re-rolled","-  ONLY the note's case id (`Case <hex> evidence note.`, 33 B) -> md5/sha1/sha256/magic differ per set; jpg 257x146, png","-  269x153, pdf 1.4, eocd 2, CD names identical across single/TT/5 Mastery sets. D9 same, plus the PE: Machine 0x014c in","-  all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). D10: the entry RVA re-rolled per variant","-  (single 0x00065bd0, TT 0x00063a80, Mastery 0x00063510 / 0x00065bd0). D11: the PE's ARCHITECTURE re-rolled per variant","-  (single 386 0x014c, TT amd64 0x8664, Mastery arm64 0xaa64 + 386) and OriginalFilename follows it (`pe-base-<goarch>.exe`).","-  D12: every dll is 5,120 B with the same layout; the MVID, the sha256 and the `Huntress.Managed.<12HEX>` type name re-roll","-  per variant (managed-001..004). D13: four installer-00N.msi with DIFFERENT bytes/sha256 (same 9,728 B) but the SAME","-  ProductCode in every mode -- the \"collision\" is the point; the answer can legitimately repeat across sets. D14: four","-  shortcut-00N.lnk, all -> `C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe` (LinkInfo and IDList agreed; \"impossible destination\" unasked).","-  Never cache a value across sets.","-- **Field-set size** -- grows AND shrinks: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 12 in every mode (Mastery","-  5 x 12); D9 13 (Mastery 5 x 13); D10 back to ONE field everywhere (Mastery 2 sets x 1, zip = the lone exe). Families: the day's field +","-  `evidence-note-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` + carry-overs","-  `d04-jpeg-*-sof-dimensions-pixels`, `d05-png-*-ihdr-dimensions-pixels`, `d06-pdf-*-header-version`, `d07-zip-*-eocd-","-  total-entries`, `d07-zip-*-central-directory-member-names`, `d09-pe-*-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`. Dispatch on the","-  answer-id SUFFIX and keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference: `challenges/day09/metadata-built-different/","-  solver/solve.py` answers all 13; `day10/metadata-where-do-we-begin/solver/solve.py` = those + entry/image-base/opt-magic","-  /ELF e_entry branches).","-- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes, case-insensitive; D9 also `0x`-hex with `trim` only,","-  so case MATTERS -> lowercase), `enum` (`accepted_values`), and since D8 `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact","-  values and order\"). Emit per `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case (`0x` yes for u16_hex, no for magic).","-- **Question-text tags** (D9 TT/Mastery, new): the first question gets ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` appended","-  (Mastery: the bundle's sha, same for every set). Strip `\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\]$` before reading a member name from question","-  text; route by `answer_id` + `artifact` instead (the D9 solver was unaffected for that reason).","-- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->","-  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.","+- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\"; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives. Container","+  NAMES drift too: D1-D14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`; D15 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding","+  `evidence-01..05.zip`. Route by the ref's text before `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.","+- **Field-set size** -- grows AND shrinks per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 single","+  1 vs TT 20 vs Mastery 100. Families: the day's field + identity + carry-overs `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`,","+  `d07-zip-*` (eocd + CD names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, version OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`,","+  `d14-lnk-*`, `d15-ooxml-*`. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX; keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference:","+  `challenges/day15/metadata-a-word-to-the-wise/solver/solve.py` answers all 20 + synthesis).","+- **Identity member roster** (D15 new) -- the kit now holds THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B,","+  `evidence-note-copy.txt` 33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B) and EACH identity question picks one at random per set:","+  ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` (`roster-sha1`,","+  `evidence-note-copy-filename`...). The filename question has artifact = the container only and asks \"the exact","+  filename of the roster\" -> map the id stem to the member whose stem matches. Never assume `evidence-note-*`.","+- **Synthesis / cross-member questions** (D15 new) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order`, kind `json`, norm","+  `case_insensitive`: \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of their","+  filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". The `artifact` names only ONE member; the real inputs are the","+  `Files:` JSON list in the question text, all in the same container. Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, resolve each","+  name under the ref's container, `hashlib.new(algo)` over the raw member bytes, sort by hex digest (descending only if","+  the text says so), emit names. Expect siblings (md5/sha1 order, size order) -- parse the algo from the id/text.","+- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree with the","+  header: always answer from the structural bytes of the member the question names.","+- **Member values** -- re-roll per variant; never cache across sets. Seen: note case id (all days); D7 entry count","+  2/3/4/5; jpg/png dimensions (D15 every set different, e.g. 423x1089, 1255x1059); D10 entry RVA; D11 PE architecture","+  (386 0x014c / amd64 0x8664 / arm64 0xaa64, OriginalFilename `pe-base-<goarch>.exe` follows); D12 MVID; D15 synthesis","+  order (driven by the re-rolled note/jpg hashes). Constant so far but don't rely on it: D13 ProductCode (identical in","+  every mode -- \"collision\" by design), D14 lnk target, D15 docx targets, the D15 kit's exe/dll/msi/lnk.","+- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),","+  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per","+  `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions.","+- **Question-text tags** -- D9 TT/Mastery appended ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` to the first question; D15","+  timed questions are prefixed ``Inspect `<member>`. `` Strip both before reading names; route by id + `artifact`.","+- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer","+  from an enclosing zip. An OOXML member is itself a zip -- parse it as the asked member, not as a wrapper to descend."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," | You see | First move |"," |---|---|","-| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | `7z l -slt <zip>` then `7z x -o work/ <zip>`; (or python `zipfile` read of the member) |","-| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the extracted member (bytes, not the zip entry name) |","+| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |","+| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |"," | \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |","-| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |","-| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |","-| `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |","-| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |","-| `zip.central_directory_*` / \"inventory every stored path, preserve directory context\" | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from EOCD cd-offset (fallback `EOCD - cd_size` if data prepended): name len u16 @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name at +46; next = +46+n+e+c. Raw stored path, CD order, no basename/dedupe/sort; decode UTF-8 (flag bit 11 `0x800`, else try UTF-8 then cp437). `7z l -slt` / `zipinfo -1` as cross-check |","-| `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |","-| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+). `xxd -s $((0x3c)) -l 4` then `xxd -s <lfanew> -l 8`. `file`/`pefile` cross-check only |","-| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` / \"start addresses\" | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (an RVA); ImageBase u32 @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). `od -An -tx4 -j$((lfanew+40)) -N4 f`. objdump's \"start address\" = ImageBase+RVA (a VA, NOT the RVA) |","-| `elf.*` / `macho.*` siblings (promised \"several architectures\", not yet asked) | ELF: `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5 picks endianness, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O: `feedface`/`feedfacf` (either byte order) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` = BE nfat_arch @4 + 20-B entries (Java .class shares `cafebabe`; small nfat_arch = fat). Emit hex in the same `0x%0Nx` width as the field's `uNN` |","-| `dotnet.*` / `.dll` \"Mono/.Net assembly\" / \"module identities\", \"rebuilds vs renames\" | CLI metadata, stdlib only (no dnfile in-window): PE data dir 14 (CLI header) -> MetaData RVA -> `BSJB` root -> stream headers (`#~`, `#Strings`, `#GUID`, `#Blob`). `#~`: HeapSizes byte @+6 (bit1 = 4-byte GUID index), Valid u64 @+8, row counts @+24; Module row 0 = Generation u16, Name (str idx), **Mvid (guid idx, 1-based)** -> 16 B at #GUID+(i-1)*16 -> `str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..))`. Cross-check: `monodis`/`ilspycmd -il` print `.module` + `// MVID: {..}` |","-| `pe.version_*` / \"version resources remember what the binaries called themselves\" | VS_VERSIONINFO StringFileInfo: `pefile.PE(data=b, fast_load=True)`; `pe.parse_data_directories(directories=[DIRECTORY_ENTRY['IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_RESOURCE']])`; walk `pe.FileInfo[..][..].StringTable[..].entries` (bytes keys). Match the id tail to the key ignoring case/`-_` (`original-filename` -> `OriginalFilename`). Shell: `strings -e l f.exe | grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |","-| `msi.*` / `.msi` / \"installers copied, renamed, repackaged\", \"stable product identities\" | OLE CFB (`d0 cf 11 e0`). Fast path: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`. Exact: CFB streams -> demangle names (0x3800-0x4840 base-64 packing) -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` (refs 3 B wide if pool header bit 0x80000000) -> `!Property` column-major (all keys, then all values). `msiinfo`/`msidump` NOT installed; `olefile` is in the venv. Reference: `challenges/day13/metadata-product-placement/solver/solve.py` `msi_property` |","-| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` / \"where each link points instead of where it sits\" | MS-SHLLINK: `4c 00 00 00` + CLSID `01140200-0000-0000-c000-000000000046`; LinkFlags u32 @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode). Target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix; Unicode offsets if LinkInfoHeaderSize >= 0x24) verbatim, else the IDList path. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` (verified D14); other lnk.* fields speculative in `lib/meta/prebuilt/lnk.py`. `LnkParse3` not needed |","-| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: a stored STRING (MSI ProductCode) verbatim, braces + uppercase; a binary GUID (.NET #GUID) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)` lowercase, no braces. answer_format (\"8-4-4-4-12 including hyphens\") does not settle braces |","-| exe-extension decoy (`.exe` that is text/zip/PNG, `MZ` with no/garbled `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | header absent -> literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit or the extension |","+| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |","+| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |","+| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |","+| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |","+| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored path, CD order, no dedupe/sort; UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else UTF-8-then-cp437 |","+| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |","+| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |","+| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |","+| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |","+| `elf.*` / `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | ELF `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O `feedface`/`feedfacf` cputype @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 |","+| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` (HeapSizes @+6, Valid @+8, rows @+24) -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |","+| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB streams -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property` (column-major). `olefile` in venv; `day13/.../solve.py msi_property` |","+| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |","+| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | it's a zip of XML parts. Relationships live in EVERY `*.rels` part (`_rels/.rels`, `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`, header/footer/settings rels). External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` (case-insensitive; absent = Internal). `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; solver: `zipfile` + ElementTree over every `.rels`, local-name `Relationship`. Core props (`docProps/core.xml`) prebuilt in `lib/meta/prebuilt/ooxml.py`; external rels NOT prebuilt as of D15 |","+| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |","+| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |","+| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |"," | \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |","-| answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |","-| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` -- compact, no spaces, no Markdown |","-| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids, artifact `delivery N: <zip> -> <member>` or `<zip>-0N.zip -> <member>` | resolve each set's member separately; see delivery layouts below |","+| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`; decide ORDER per field (conventions) |","+| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |"," "," ## Day by day","-**Days 1-8** (one field each, all first-try ~27-57 s unless noted): D1 identity (filename/size/md5/sha1/sha256; Mastery","-zip-of-zips first seen) -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` (TT `readme.exe` was text, Mastery `.bin` a PDF; stale question member ->","-`find_artifact_hinted`) -> D3 `text.utf8_bom_present` (`*-with-bom.txt` really had one -- bytes, not name) -> D4 JPEG SOFn","-`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR `<w>x<h>` -> D6 `pdf.header_version` bare `x.y` (Mastery two same-named `delivery N:` downloads) -> D7","-`zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip (stdlib EOCD parse; TT 3, Mastery 4/5) -> D8 `zip.central_directory_member_names`","-compact JSON of full CD paths in CD order (5-member kit, 12 fields).","+**Days 1-8** (one field each, first try ~27-57 s): D1 identity (Mastery zip-of-zips first seen) -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16`","+(TT `readme.exe` was text) -> D3 `text.utf8_bom_present` -> D4 JPEG SOFn `<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6","+`pdf.header_version` bare `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 `zip.central_directory_member_names`","+compact JSON in CD order (5-member kit, 12 fields)."," ","-**Days 9-11** (one Go 1.22 PE, `d09-pe-NNN-...`): D9 `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `0x014c` (padded u16; not the binary","-lane's `i386`), ~47 s. D10 `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` (u32 @ e_lfanew+40) `0x%08x` -> `0x00065bd0`; unpadded","-`0x65bd0` REJECTED (objdump's start address is the VA), ~75 s, 1 wrong. D11 `pe.version_original_filename` =","-VS_VERSIONINFO OriginalFilename verbatim (`pe-base-386.exe`, not the randomized member name), pefile walk, ~25 s. All","-TT/Mastery first try (RVA / GOARCH re-rolled per variant).","+**Days 9-11** (one Go PE, `d09-pe-NNN-...`): D9 `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c` (~47 s). D10","+`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` `0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED, ~75 s). D11 `pe.version_original_filename` verbatim","+(`pe-base-386.exe`, ~25 s). All TT/Mastery first try."," ","-**Day 12 — Managed Expectations** (`dotnet.mvid_guid`, `pattern` \"canonical GUID text in 8-4-4-4-12 ... including","-hyphens\", id `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid`): 5,120 B PE32 .NET `managed-001.dll`. MVID = Module row 0 Mvid (1-based","-#GUID index) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)` lowercase, no braces (`21e410f3-c977-465c-...`). The worker typed a ~90-line","-stdlib PE -> CLI header -> BSJB -> `#~` -> `#GUID` parser (~55 s, first try). TT/Mastery 2 sets first try. Parser now","-`lib/meta/dotnet.py`. \"Renames vs rebuilds\" was never asked.","+**Days 12-14** (one new member family each, 1 field everywhere, TT 1 / Mastery 2x1, all timed first try):","+D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` -- 5 KB .NET dll, #GUID heap -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le)` lowercase no braces, ~55 s. D13","+`msi.product_code_guid` -- 9.7 KB MSI, Property table ProductCode VERBATIM with braces (brace-less REJECTED), ~76 s. D14","+`lnk.target_path_windows` -- 547 B LNK, LinkInfo LocalBasePath `C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe`, ~40 s (prebuilt key was","+`target_path`, one suffix short -> worker re-typed the parser)."," ","-**Day 13 — Product Placement** (`msi.product_code_guid`, kind `pattern` \"canonical GUID text in 8-4-4-4-12 hexadecimal","-form, including hyphens\", norm `trim`, id `d13-msi-001-msi-product-code-guid`). Prompt: \"Installers were copied, renamed,","-and repackaged. Recover stable product identities, distinguish revisions from different products, and find the collision.\"","-- Artifact: 3.3 KB zip -> `installer-001.msi` (9,728 B, msitools 0.103 OLE/CFB with an embedded `artifact.cab`).","-- Key insight: answer = Property table `ProductCode` row VERBATIM `{DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61}`. Decoys in the","-  same file: UpgradeCode, Component.ComponentId, SummaryInformation RevisionNumber (= PackageCode).","-- Worker: stdlib CFB + MSI string-pool reader (regex `ProductCode(\\{...\\})` fallback). First submit stripped the braces","-  (answer_format never mentions them) -> REJECTED; braced -> CORRECT. Start -> CORRECT ~76 s, 1 wrong (~19 s lost).","-- TT (50 s window, in_window 0.96 s) and Mastery 2 sets (80 s, 2.55 s) CORRECT first try; every variant had the same","-  ProductCode. \"Revisions vs products\" / \"collision\" were never asked -- only the ProductCode.","+**Day 15 — A Word to the Wise** (`ooxml.external_relationship_targets`, kind `json` \"compact valid JSON array with exact","+values and order\", norm `trim`, id `d15-ooxml-001-ooxml-external-relationship-targets`). Prompt: \"Office documents","+contain relationships that point beyond the page. Separate internal references from external dependencies and find","+the document reaching somewhere it should not.\"","+- Artifact: 1,316 B zip -> `document-15-001.docx` (3,803 B; 5 parts: `[Content_Types].xml`, `_rels/.rels`,","+  `docProps/core.xml`, `word/document.xml`, `word/_rels/document.xml.rels`). The package rels are Internal","+  (officeDocument, core-properties); `document.xml.rels` holds two `hyperlink` rels `rId9` -> `https://example.test/","+  evidence/<token>` and `rId10` -> `https://example.test/control`, both `TargetMode=\"External\"`, referenced from","+  `<w:hyperlink r:id=..>` in body order rId9, rId10.","+- Key insight: answer = the Target strings of every External relationship, as a compact JSON array SORTED ASCENDING","+  (`[\"https://example.test/control\",\"https://example.test/evidence/<token>\"]`). The rels-file / body order (rId9 first)","+  was REJECTED. Caveat: sorted-by-Target and sorted-by-Id-as-string (`rId10` < `rId9`) coincide here -- sort by Target.","+- Single: start -> wrong submit at +24 s (file order) -> CORRECT at +50 s. 1 wrong, ~26 s lost.","+- TT: the 12-member kit (note, `evidence-note-copy.txt`, `roster.csv`, jpg, png, pdf, evidence-drop zip, exe, dll, msi,","+  lnk, docx) with 20 fields incl. the new identity-member roster and `metadata-day-15-synthesis-sha256-order`. The","+  shipped solver didn't answer the synthesis id; offline generalize added `_digest_order` (above). TT CORRECT 20/20,","+  in-window 1.72 s (solve 0.27 s). Mastery 5 sets x 20 = 100 CORRECT first submit, in-window 1.83 s (solve 0.44 s)."," ","-**Day 14 — The Shortcut Home** (`lnk.target_path_windows`, kind `exact_text`, \"use the literal none only when the","-requested field is absent\", norm `trim`, id `d14-lnk-001-lnk-target-path-windows`). Prompt: \"A shortcut collection is a","-map of intent -- if you read where each link points instead of where it sits. Reconstruct the targets and identify the","-impossible destination.\"","-- Artifact: 475 B zip -> `shortcut-001.lnk` (547 B; LinkFlags 0x97: IDList + LinkInfo + Name + WorkingDir + Unicode).","-- Key insight: answer = LinkInfo LocalBasePath VERBATIM (`C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe`); the IDList (volume item +","-  file-entry items, long names from the 0xBEEF0004 extension) spelled the same. Not the WorkingDir (`C:\\Windows\\System32`).","-- Worker: the lane solver (`lib.meta`) answered `(None, None)` -- prebuilt `lib/meta/prebuilt/lnk.py` registered","-  `lnk.target_path` but NOT the asked `target_path_windows`, so the exact-key lookup missed. The worker typed a ~70-line","-  LinkInfo/IDList reader into `local_answer()` and submitted; start -> CORRECT ~40 s, first try (3 tool calls).","-- TT (shortcut-002) and Mastery 2 sets (003/004, nested `-01.zip` holding `-01/-02.zip`) CORRECT first try, solve <0.1 s.","-- LIB (ratchet D14): `lib/meta/lnk.py:target_path` registered verified as (`lnk`, `target_path_windows`), days=(14,).","-"," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.","-- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).","-- Booleans: enum `true` / `false` (lowercase) — the contract hands the vocabulary; pick, don't probe.","-- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both,","-  re-confirmed D8 `257x146` / `269x153`).","-- PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`","-  (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).","-- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 + D8 all modes).","-- JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path","-  with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).","-  Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.","-- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine ->","-  `0x014c` (D9), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint -> `0x00065bd0` (D10, all modes). The width comes from the STRUCT, not the id","-  (D10's id has no `u32`). Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`), and the","-  binary lane's `entry_point` was accepted UNPADDED (`0x401040`) -- different lane, different generator.","-- GUIDs (`dotnet.mvid_guid`): .NET `Guid.ToString()` form -- first 3 groups byte-swapped from the heap bytes (bytes_le),","-  lowercase, hyphenated, no braces (D12 all modes; `knowledge.DOTNET_MVID_GUID`, playbook metadata `guid` entry).","-- MSI GUIDs (`msi.product_code_guid`): the Property string VERBATIM -- uppercase WITH braces `{DD1A80D5-...}` (D13 all","-  modes; `knowledge.MSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID`). Bare form REJECTED. GUID spelling follows the source, not answer_format.","-- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): the stored LinkInfo path verbatim -- backslashes, original case, drive","-  letter, no quotes (D14 all modes; `knowledge.LNK_TARGET_PATH_WINDOWS`, playbook metadata `windows`/`path` entry).","-- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): the StringFileInfo value verbatim, incl. extension (`pe-base-386.exe`,","-  D11 all modes). `knowledge.PE_VERSION_STRING_KEY` maps id tail -> resource key.","-- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` for pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex (D10 single; unpadded); brace-less","-  `DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61` for msi.product_code_guid (D13 single).","-- `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`,","-  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `PE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT`, `PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT` (+`_REJECTED`), `BOOL`;","-  `playbook` metadata `hex` entry carries the padding rule.","-- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,","-  `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD","-  file-name fields, `coff_machine_u16_hex` = COFF FileHeader.Machine as u16 hex) — read the field name literally to","-  pick which structure to parse; a claimed count is NOT a CD walk / `zipfile` len, and CD names are NOT local-header","-  names (they happened to agree on D7/D8). A `_uNN_hex` suffix fixes both the read width and the printed width.","+- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.","+- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase `x`, no spaces.","+- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.","+- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:","+  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).","+  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.","+  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15 TT/Mastery; norm `case_insensitive`).","+  Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk","+  order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.","+- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine","+  `0x014c`, u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT, not the id. (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`;","+  the binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)","+- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces","+  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.","+- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes).","+- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension.","+- URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups.","+- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15).","+- `knowledge.py` holds the format constants (`JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT` ... `PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT`, `DOTNET_MVID_GUID`,","+  `MSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID`, `LNK_TARGET_PATH_WINDOWS`, `BOOL`); `playbook` metadata entries carry hex/guid/path rules.","+- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,","+  `external_relationship_targets` = rels `Target` where `TargetMode=External`) -- read it literally to pick the","+  structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width."," "," ## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)","-- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (D8: 5 members, filename question's artifact = zip only).","-- Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and","-  `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.","-- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked","-  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).","-- Mastery day 8: same shape, FIVE sets: one 17 KB download `metadata-day-08-evidence-01.zip` (Stored, UTF-8 flag) holding","-  `-01.zip`..`-05.zip`, each a full 5-member kit (incl. its own `evidence-drop-001.zip`). Refs `...-evidence-0N.zip ->","-  <member>`; every set reuses the same member names, so resolve by (set zip, member), never member name alone.","-- Mastery day 9: same five-set shape, but the GM download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip`","-  (`metadata-forensics-day-09-built-different-mastery.zip`, 2.99 MB, Stored) while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip","-  -> <member>` -- resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not by its filename.","-- Mastery day 10: TWO sets only, refs `metadata-day-10-evidence-0N.zip -> telemetry-agent-00N.exe` (003/004).","-  Day 11 identical shape (`metadata-day-11-evidence-0N.zip`, one download nesting both set zips).","-- Mastery day 14: two sets, one download `metadata-day-14-evidence-01.zip` nesting `-01.zip`/`-02.zip`, refs","-  `metadata-day-14-evidence-0N.zip -> shortcut-00N.lnk` (003/004).","-- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.","-- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.","+- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only).","+- Mastery zip-of-zips (days 1,2,4,5,7,8,10,11,14,15): ONE download (`...-evidence-01.zip`; D15 `evidence-01.zip`)","+  holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip`, each holding its set's member(s) (D7 three levels; D8/D15 five full kits, D15 ~606 KB","+  each). Refs `<set zip> -> <member>`; every set reuses member names -> resolve by (set zip, member).","+- Mastery day 9: download named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip` ->","+  resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not its filename.","+- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` refs.","+- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) -- never hardcode names."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") — recurse into nested zips.","-- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.","-- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation/provenance, but only the","-  named field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.","-- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence","-  zip reads the OUTER EOCD / CD (D8 outer CD = the 5 kit members, Mastery outer = 5 set zips). Resolve the named member's","-  bytes first, then parse.","-- Name-list fields: `zipfile.namelist()` is CD order but decodes non-UTF-8-flagged names as cp437 and is fine for honest","-  zips; for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `C:\\`, `\\` separators, LFH != CD name, duplicates) emit the CD bytes as-is --","-  don't let an extractor's sanitizing (7z/unzip strip `../` and leading `/`) rewrite the answer.","-- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.","-- Timed windows are ~5-10 s (D8: TT 8 s / Mastery 10 s; D9 shrank to 6 s / 7 s) and most of it is GM start/download/","-  submit round-trips (D9 TT submit alone 2.3 s): never do anything slow (extraction to disk, exiftool, `pefile` full","-  parse, subprocess) in-window; parse fixed offsets in memory. Big members (1.2 MB exe x5) pushed Mastery solve to 0.86 s","-  -- decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member).","-- A prebuilt registry key that is one suffix short is a miss (D14: prebuilt `lnk.target_path`, GM asked","-  `target_path_windows` -> the worker re-typed the parser; most of D14's ~40 s). When a format is prebuilt, `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as","-  m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and call the nearest extractor directly before writing one.","-- Fresh member family = skeleton solver (D10, D12): copy the previous day's solver first, then add the new family's","-  handler -- D12's worker re-typed the identity/PE branches next to the .NET parser (~50 s of generation).","-- Executable fields: don't take `file`'s \"Intel i386\" / `pefile` machine names / the Go GOARCH token as the answer; the","-  metadata field is the raw u16. And require `PE\\0\\0` exactly at e_lfanew -- an `MZ` stub alone is not a PE (decoy).","-- Normalizing a stored value (D13, cost a wrong submit + 19 s): the solver's `_guid()` stripped MSI braces because","-  answer_format said \"8-4-4-4-12\". When the field is a stored string, emit it verbatim; reshape only what the format","-  explicitly forbids.","-- Hex width (D10, cost a wrong submit + 17 s): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x` for the field's","-  struct size. RVA vs VA: `_rva` = the raw field, never ImageBase + it.","-- Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and","-  add only the new suffix handler -- D8 27 s, D9 47 s that way. The harness skeleton in `solver/solve.py` is NOT the","-  previous day's solver; `cp challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py` over it (D10 spliced by sed instead).","-- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` (with ids, no sha tag) but","-  NO `answer_ids` -- `jq '.answer_ids|map(..)'` errors; read `questions[].id` to preview the field set.","-- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` and made the stop gate","-  think it was incomplete (Day 2, ~2 min lost) — restore start.json from `log.jsonl`.","-- Tools installed (2026-10-07): exiftool, pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler), qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck,","-  zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo, sqlite3, identify/convert (ImageMagick), olevba/oleid.","+- JSON list ORDER (D15, 1 wrong + ~26 s): \"exact values and order\" does not say WHICH order. File order was rejected","+  for rels targets; sorted won. Decide per field (conventions above) before the first submit.","+- Timed field set != single field set (D15): single asked 1 field, TT 20 incl. an unseen synthesis question and","+  re-rolled identity members -> the shipped solver missed one id. Keep the cumulative solver (identity for ANY member","+  stem, every carry-over family) in place before the timed run, and treat any `synthesis`/\"Files: [...]\" question as","+  a computed cross-member answer, not a lookup.","+- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") -- recurse.","+- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (D2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.","+- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: only the named field is graded; extra checks are diagnostics.","+- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded zip reads the OUTER EOCD. Resolve the named","+  member's bytes first, then parse (same for OOXML: open the docx member, not the evidence zip).","+- Name-list fields: emit CD bytes as-is for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `\\`, duplicates) -- extractors sanitize.","+- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF -- bytes win every time.","+- Timed windows are seconds; most of it is GM round-trips (D15 start 1.0 s + submit 1.1 s). Parse in memory, never","+  shell out/extract to disk in-window; decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member) (1.2 MB exe x5).","+- A prebuilt registry key one suffix short is a miss (D14 `lnk.target_path` vs `target_path_windows`). Check","+  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and call the nearest","+  extractor directly before writing one.","+- Fresh member family = copy the previous day's solver first (it answers every earlier family), then add only the new","+  handler -- D8 27 s / D9 47 s that way; re-typing older branches cost D12 ~50 s.","+- Normalizing a stored value (D13): don't strip braces/reshape a stored string because answer_format sounds generic.","+- Hex width (D10): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x`. `_rva` = raw field, never ImageBase + it.","+- Executable fields: the metadata field is the raw u16, not `file`/`pefile`/GOARCH names; require `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew.","+- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` but NO `answer_ids`.","+- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on a solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` (D2, ~2 min lost) --","+  restore from `log.jsonl`.","+- Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,","+  mediainfo, sqlite3, ImageMagick, olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile. Not installed: msitools, LnkParse3, dnfile."]}],"originalFile":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-14; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny\n  member (33 B - 3 KB) and ONE structural fact. Day 8+: the zip carries the whole cumulative kit (note + jpg + png + pdf +\n  inner zip [+ D9 a 1.26 MB PE `.exe`]) and even the SINGLE contract asks every field (D8 12, D9 13 = identity + every\n  earlier day's field + the new one). The member can itself be a container (D7/8: an inner ZIP whose own EOCD / CD is\n  the asked field). Each day adds ONE member + ONE field; the previous kit members are byte-identical except the case id.\n- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only\n  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`). Day 10 stayed on the SAME\n  PE (`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`) and DE-escalated: zip = the exe only, contract = 1 field (TT 1, Mastery 2x1).\n  Day 11 kept that shape and moved INTO the PE's resources (`pe.version_original_filename`, VS_VERSIONINFO string).\n  Day 12 switched to a NEW member family -- a 5 KB .NET dll (`d12-dotnet-NNN-dotnet-mvid-guid`) -- and went into the CLI\n  METADATA tables (Module.Mvid via the #GUID heap); same 1-field / TT 1 / Mastery 2x1 shape. Day 13 another NEW\n  family -- a 9.7 KB MSI (OLE/CFB, `d13-msi-NNN-msi-product-code-guid`) -> the Property table; same 1-field shape.\n  Day 14 another NEW family -- a 547 B Windows shortcut (`d14-lnk-NNN-lnk-target-path-windows`) -> LinkInfo; same shape.\n- A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->\n  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` ->\n  `zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` ->\n  `pe.version_original_filename` -> `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows`. Since Day 3 the question literally names the field\n  (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`). NOTE the\n  `dNN` is the drop/member family, not the day the field appeared: Day 8's new field came as `d07-zip-001-zip-central-\n  directory-member-names`; Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`); Day 10's as `d09-pe-001-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex` (same exe family), Day 11's as\n  `d09-pe-001-pe-version-original-filename`, Day 12's as `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid` (new family -> new `dNN`).\n- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk\n  \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides, \"impossible provenance\" names). The asked field so far was always the\n  STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Singles D1-D9 were\n  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; D10 took one wrong spelling (unpadded hex). Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT first try.\n- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9: \"executables for several architectures, plus decoys wearing\n  executable extensions\" -> one honest i386 PE, no ELF/Mach-O/decoy in any mode). Expect the promised cases to arrive\n  later as mutations; pre-arm the sibling parsers (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing their spellings.\n- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree\n  with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.\n- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is\n  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`). Day 8 re-rolled\n  ONLY the note's case id (`Case <hex> evidence note.`, 33 B) -> md5/sha1/sha256/magic differ per set; jpg 257x146, png\n  269x153, pdf 1.4, eocd 2, CD names identical across single/TT/5 Mastery sets. D9 same, plus the PE: Machine 0x014c in\n  all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). D10: the entry RVA re-rolled per variant\n  (single 0x00065bd0, TT 0x00063a80, Mastery 0x00063510 / 0x00065bd0). D11: the PE's ARCHITECTURE re-rolled per variant\n  (single 386 0x014c, TT amd64 0x8664, Mastery arm64 0xaa64 + 386) and OriginalFilename follows it (`pe-base-<goarch>.exe`).\n  D12: every dll is 5,120 B with the same layout; the MVID, the sha256 and the `Huntress.Managed.<12HEX>` type name re-roll\n  per variant (managed-001..004). D13: four installer-00N.msi with DIFFERENT bytes/sha256 (same 9,728 B) but the SAME\n  ProductCode in every mode -- the \"collision\" is the point; the answer can legitimately repeat across sets. D14: four\n  shortcut-00N.lnk, all -> `C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe` (LinkInfo and IDList agreed; \"impossible destination\" unasked).\n  Never cache a value across sets.\n- **Field-set size** -- grows AND shrinks: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 12 in every mode (Mastery\n  5 x 12); D9 13 (Mastery 5 x 13); D10 back to ONE field everywhere (Mastery 2 sets x 1, zip = the lone exe). Families: the day's field +\n  `evidence-note-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` + carry-overs\n  `d04-jpeg-*-sof-dimensions-pixels`, `d05-png-*-ihdr-dimensions-pixels`, `d06-pdf-*-header-version`, `d07-zip-*-eocd-\n  total-entries`, `d07-zip-*-central-directory-member-names`, `d09-pe-*-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`. Dispatch on the\n  answer-id SUFFIX and keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference: `challenges/day09/metadata-built-different/\n  solver/solve.py` answers all 13; `day10/metadata-where-do-we-begin/solver/solve.py` = those + entry/image-base/opt-magic\n  /ELF e_entry branches).\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes, case-insensitive; D9 also `0x`-hex with `trim` only,\n  so case MATTERS -> lowercase), `enum` (`accepted_values`), and since D8 `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact\n  values and order\"). Emit per `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case (`0x` yes for u16_hex, no for magic).\n- **Question-text tags** (D9 TT/Mastery, new): the first question gets ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` appended\n  (Mastery: the bundle's sha, same for every set). Strip `\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\]$` before reading a member name from question\n  text; route by `answer_id` + `artifact` instead (the D9 solver was unaffected for that reason).\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | `7z l -slt <zip>` then `7z x -o work/ <zip>`; (or python `zipfile` read of the member) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the extracted member (bytes, not the zip entry name) |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |\n| `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` / \"inventory every stored path, preserve directory context\" | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from EOCD cd-offset (fallback `EOCD - cd_size` if data prepended): name len u16 @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name at +46; next = +46+n+e+c. Raw stored path, CD order, no basename/dedupe/sort; decode UTF-8 (flag bit 11 `0x800`, else try UTF-8 then cp437). `7z l -slt` / `zipinfo -1` as cross-check |\n| `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |\n| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+). `xxd -s $((0x3c)) -l 4` then `xxd -s <lfanew> -l 8`. `file`/`pefile` cross-check only |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` / \"start addresses\" | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (an RVA); ImageBase u32 @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). `od -An -tx4 -j$((lfanew+40)) -N4 f`. objdump's \"start address\" = ImageBase+RVA (a VA, NOT the RVA) |\n| `elf.*` / `macho.*` siblings (promised \"several architectures\", not yet asked) | ELF: `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5 picks endianness, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O: `feedface`/`feedfacf` (either byte order) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` = BE nfat_arch @4 + 20-B entries (Java .class shares `cafebabe`; small nfat_arch = fat). Emit hex in the same `0x%0Nx` width as the field's `uNN` |\n| `dotnet.*` / `.dll` \"Mono/.Net assembly\" / \"module identities\", \"rebuilds vs renames\" | CLI metadata, stdlib only (no dnfile in-window): PE data dir 14 (CLI header) -> MetaData RVA -> `BSJB` root -> stream headers (`#~`, `#Strings`, `#GUID`, `#Blob`). `#~`: HeapSizes byte @+6 (bit1 = 4-byte GUID index), Valid u64 @+8, row counts @+24; Module row 0 = Generation u16, Name (str idx), **Mvid (guid idx, 1-based)** -> 16 B at #GUID+(i-1)*16 -> `str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..))`. Cross-check: `monodis`/`ilspycmd -il` print `.module` + `// MVID: {..}` |\n| `pe.version_*` / \"version resources remember what the binaries called themselves\" | VS_VERSIONINFO StringFileInfo: `pefile.PE(data=b, fast_load=True)`; `pe.parse_data_directories(directories=[DIRECTORY_ENTRY['IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_RESOURCE']])`; walk `pe.FileInfo[..][..].StringTable[..].entries` (bytes keys). Match the id tail to the key ignoring case/`-_` (`original-filename` -> `OriginalFilename`). Shell: `strings -e l f.exe | grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| `msi.*` / `.msi` / \"installers copied, renamed, repackaged\", \"stable product identities\" | OLE CFB (`d0 cf 11 e0`). Fast path: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`. Exact: CFB streams -> demangle names (0x3800-0x4840 base-64 packing) -> `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` (refs 3 B wide if pool header bit 0x80000000) -> `!Property` column-major (all keys, then all values). `msiinfo`/`msidump` NOT installed; `olefile` is in the venv. Reference: `challenges/day13/metadata-product-placement/solver/solve.py` `msi_property` |\n| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` / \"where each link points instead of where it sits\" | MS-SHLLINK: `4c 00 00 00` + CLSID `01140200-0000-0000-c000-000000000046`; LinkFlags u32 @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode). Target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix; Unicode offsets if LinkInfoHeaderSize >= 0x24) verbatim, else the IDList path. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` (verified D14); other lnk.* fields speculative in `lib/meta/prebuilt/lnk.py`. `LnkParse3` not needed |\n| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: a stored STRING (MSI ProductCode) verbatim, braces + uppercase; a binary GUID (.NET #GUID) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)` lowercase, no braces. answer_format (\"8-4-4-4-12 including hyphens\") does not settle braces |\n| exe-extension decoy (`.exe` that is text/zip/PNG, `MZ` with no/garbled `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | header absent -> literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit or the extension |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` -- compact, no spaces, no Markdown |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids, artifact `delivery N: <zip> -> <member>` or `<zip>-0N.zip -> <member>` | resolve each set's member separately; see delivery layouts below |\n\n## Day by day\n**Days 1-8** (one field each, all first-try ~27-57 s unless noted): D1 identity (filename/size/md5/sha1/sha256; Mastery\nzip-of-zips first seen) -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` (TT `readme.exe` was text, Mastery `.bin` a PDF; stale question member ->\n`find_artifact_hinted`) -> D3 `text.utf8_bom_present` (`*-with-bom.txt` really had one -- bytes, not name) -> D4 JPEG SOFn\n`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR `<w>x<h>` -> D6 `pdf.header_version` bare `x.y` (Mastery two same-named `delivery N:` downloads) -> D7\n`zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip (stdlib EOCD parse; TT 3, Mastery 4/5) -> D8 `zip.central_directory_member_names`\ncompact JSON of full CD paths in CD order (5-member kit, 12 fields).\n\n**Days 9-11** (one Go 1.22 PE, `d09-pe-NNN-...`): D9 `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `0x014c` (padded u16; not the binary\nlane's `i386`), ~47 s. D10 `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` (u32 @ e_lfanew+40) `0x%08x` -> `0x00065bd0`; unpadded\n`0x65bd0` REJECTED (objdump's start address is the VA), ~75 s, 1 wrong. D11 `pe.version_original_filename` =\nVS_VERSIONINFO OriginalFilename verbatim (`pe-base-386.exe`, not the randomized member name), pefile walk, ~25 s. All\nTT/Mastery first try (RVA / GOARCH re-rolled per variant).\n\n**Day 12 — Managed Expectations** (`dotnet.mvid_guid`, `pattern` \"canonical GUID text in 8-4-4-4-12 ... including\nhyphens\", id `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid`): 5,120 B PE32 .NET `managed-001.dll`. MVID = Module row 0 Mvid (1-based\n#GUID index) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)` lowercase, no braces (`21e410f3-c977-465c-...`). The worker typed a ~90-line\nstdlib PE -> CLI header -> BSJB -> `#~` -> `#GUID` parser (~55 s, first try). TT/Mastery 2 sets first try. Parser now\n`lib/meta/dotnet.py`. \"Renames vs rebuilds\" was never asked.\n\n**Day 13 — Product Placement** (`msi.product_code_guid`, kind `pattern` \"canonical GUID text in 8-4-4-4-12 hexadecimal\nform, including hyphens\", norm `trim`, id `d13-msi-001-msi-product-code-guid`). Prompt: \"Installers were copied, renamed,\nand repackaged. Recover stable product identities, distinguish revisions from different products, and find the collision.\"\n- Artifact: 3.3 KB zip -> `installer-001.msi` (9,728 B, msitools 0.103 OLE/CFB with an embedded `artifact.cab`).\n- Key insight: answer = Property table `ProductCode` row VERBATIM `{DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61}`. Decoys in the\n  same file: UpgradeCode, Component.ComponentId, SummaryInformation RevisionNumber (= PackageCode).\n- Worker: stdlib CFB + MSI string-pool reader (regex `ProductCode(\\{...\\})` fallback). First submit stripped the braces\n  (answer_format never mentions them) -> REJECTED; braced -> CORRECT. Start -> CORRECT ~76 s, 1 wrong (~19 s lost).\n- TT (50 s window, in_window 0.96 s) and Mastery 2 sets (80 s, 2.55 s) CORRECT first try; every variant had the same\n  ProductCode. \"Revisions vs products\" / \"collision\" were never asked -- only the ProductCode.\n\n**Day 14 — The Shortcut Home** (`lnk.target_path_windows`, kind `exact_text`, \"use the literal none only when the\nrequested field is absent\", norm `trim`, id `d14-lnk-001-lnk-target-path-windows`). Prompt: \"A shortcut collection is a\nmap of intent -- if you read where each link points instead of where it sits. Reconstruct the targets and identify the\nimpossible destination.\"\n- Artifact: 475 B zip -> `shortcut-001.lnk` (547 B; LinkFlags 0x97: IDList + LinkInfo + Name + WorkingDir + Unicode).\n- Key insight: answer = LinkInfo LocalBasePath VERBATIM (`C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe`); the IDList (volume item +\n  file-entry items, long names from the 0xBEEF0004 extension) spelled the same. Not the WorkingDir (`C:\\Windows\\System32`).\n- Worker: the lane solver (`lib.meta`) answered `(None, None)` -- prebuilt `lib/meta/prebuilt/lnk.py` registered\n  `lnk.target_path` but NOT the asked `target_path_windows`, so the exact-key lookup missed. The worker typed a ~70-line\n  LinkInfo/IDList reader into `local_answer()` and submitted; start -> CORRECT ~40 s, first try (3 tool calls).\n- TT (shortcut-002) and Mastery 2 sets (003/004, nested `-01.zip` holding `-01/-02.zip`) CORRECT first try, solve <0.1 s.\n- LIB (ratchet D14): `lib/meta/lnk.py:target_path` registered verified as (`lnk`, `target_path_windows`), days=(14,).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).\n- Booleans: enum `true` / `false` (lowercase) — the contract hands the vocabulary; pick, don't probe.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both,\n  re-confirmed D8 `257x146` / `269x153`).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`\n  (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).\n- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 + D8 all modes).\n- JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path\n  with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).\n  Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.\n- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine ->\n  `0x014c` (D9), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint -> `0x00065bd0` (D10, all modes). The width comes from the STRUCT, not the id\n  (D10's id has no `u32`). Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`), and the\n  binary lane's `entry_point` was accepted UNPADDED (`0x401040`) -- different lane, different generator.\n- GUIDs (`dotnet.mvid_guid`): .NET `Guid.ToString()` form -- first 3 groups byte-swapped from the heap bytes (bytes_le),\n  lowercase, hyphenated, no braces (D12 all modes; `knowledge.DOTNET_MVID_GUID`, playbook metadata `guid` entry).\n- MSI GUIDs (`msi.product_code_guid`): the Property string VERBATIM -- uppercase WITH braces `{DD1A80D5-...}` (D13 all\n  modes; `knowledge.MSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID`). Bare form REJECTED. GUID spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): the stored LinkInfo path verbatim -- backslashes, original case, drive\n  letter, no quotes (D14 all modes; `knowledge.LNK_TARGET_PATH_WINDOWS`, playbook metadata `windows`/`path` entry).\n- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): the StringFileInfo value verbatim, incl. extension (`pe-base-386.exe`,\n  D11 all modes). `knowledge.PE_VERSION_STRING_KEY` maps id tail -> resource key.\n- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` for pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex (D10 single; unpadded); brace-less\n  `DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61` for msi.product_code_guid (D13 single).\n- `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`,\n  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `PE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT`, `PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT` (+`_REJECTED`), `BOOL`;\n  `playbook` metadata `hex` entry carries the padding rule.\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,\n  `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD\n  file-name fields, `coff_machine_u16_hex` = COFF FileHeader.Machine as u16 hex) — read the field name literally to\n  pick which structure to parse; a claimed count is NOT a CD walk / `zipfile` len, and CD names are NOT local-header\n  names (they happened to agree on D7/D8). A `_uNN_hex` suffix fixes both the read width and the printed width.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (D8: 5 members, filename question's artifact = zip only).\n- Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and\n  `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.\n- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked\n  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).\n- Mastery day 8: same shape, FIVE sets: one 17 KB download `metadata-day-08-evidence-01.zip` (Stored, UTF-8 flag) holding\n  `-01.zip`..`-05.zip`, each a full 5-member kit (incl. its own `evidence-drop-001.zip`). Refs `...-evidence-0N.zip ->\n  <member>`; every set reuses the same member names, so resolve by (set zip, member), never member name alone.\n- Mastery day 9: same five-set shape, but the GM download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip`\n  (`metadata-forensics-day-09-built-different-mastery.zip`, 2.99 MB, Stored) while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip\n  -> <member>` -- resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not by its filename.\n- Mastery day 10: TWO sets only, refs `metadata-day-10-evidence-0N.zip -> telemetry-agent-00N.exe` (003/004).\n  Day 11 identical shape (`metadata-day-11-evidence-0N.zip`, one download nesting both set zips).\n- Mastery day 14: two sets, one download `metadata-day-14-evidence-01.zip` nesting `-01.zip`/`-02.zip`, refs\n  `metadata-day-14-evidence-0N.zip -> shortcut-00N.lnk` (003/004).\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") — recurse into nested zips.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation/provenance, but only the\n  named field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence\n  zip reads the OUTER EOCD / CD (D8 outer CD = the 5 kit members, Mastery outer = 5 set zips). Resolve the named member's\n  bytes first, then parse.\n- Name-list fields: `zipfile.namelist()` is CD order but decodes non-UTF-8-flagged names as cp437 and is fine for honest\n  zips; for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `C:\\`, `\\` separators, LFH != CD name, duplicates) emit the CD bytes as-is --\n  don't let an extractor's sanitizing (7z/unzip strip `../` and leading `/`) rewrite the answer.\n- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are ~5-10 s (D8: TT 8 s / Mastery 10 s; D9 shrank to 6 s / 7 s) and most of it is GM start/download/\n  submit round-trips (D9 TT submit alone 2.3 s): never do anything slow (extraction to disk, exiftool, `pefile` full\n  parse, subprocess) in-window; parse fixed offsets in memory. Big members (1.2 MB exe x5) pushed Mastery solve to 0.86 s\n  -- decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member).\n- A prebuilt registry key that is one suffix short is a miss (D14: prebuilt `lnk.target_path`, GM asked\n  `target_path_windows` -> the worker re-typed the parser; most of D14's ~40 s). When a format is prebuilt, `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as\n  m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and call the nearest extractor directly before writing one.\n- Fresh member family = skeleton solver (D10, D12): copy the previous day's solver first, then add the new family's\n  handler -- D12's worker re-typed the identity/PE branches next to the .NET parser (~50 s of generation).\n- Executable fields: don't take `file`'s \"Intel i386\" / `pefile` machine names / the Go GOARCH token as the answer; the\n  metadata field is the raw u16. And require `PE\\0\\0` exactly at e_lfanew -- an `MZ` stub alone is not a PE (decoy).\n- Normalizing a stored value (D13, cost a wrong submit + 19 s): the solver's `_guid()` stripped MSI braces because\n  answer_format said \"8-4-4-4-12\". When the field is a stored string, emit it verbatim; reshape only what the format\n  explicitly forbids.\n- Hex width (D10, cost a wrong submit + 17 s): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x` for the field's\n  struct size. RVA vs VA: `_rva` = the raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n- Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and\n  add only the new suffix handler -- D8 27 s, D9 47 s that way. The harness skeleton in `solver/solve.py` is NOT the\n  previous day's solver; `cp challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py` over it (D10 spliced by sed instead).\n- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` (with ids, no sha tag) but\n  NO `answer_ids` -- `jq '.answer_ids|map(..)'` errors; read `questions[].id` to preview the field set.\n- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` and made the stop gate\n  think it was incomplete (Day 2, ~2 min lost) — restore start.json from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed (2026-10-07): exiftool, pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler), qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck,\n  zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo, sqlite3, identify/convert (ImageMagick), olevba/oleid.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Diw1AQBLwT3VuyWDYeyhJ2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
